[0.10.0]
- Feature: "Fixed costs" report — every transaction tagged "monthly recurring expense",
  rolled up per month. Sits under the period summary, collapsed by default,
  open state kept in the URL (?fixed=1)
- Shows the month's total, item count, share of income, and the 12-month average
- Per-item table grouped by bill → payee → description, with the expected amount
  (6-month median), last charge date, and a flag when a charge drifts >5% from its median
- Flags recurring items not yet booked this month, once their usual due day has passed
- 12-month bar strip; click a bar to re-anchor the report to that month
- Transfers count toward fixed costs (a paycheck arrives as a transfer here, so
  transfers are real money movements); tagged deposits are ignored and flagged as
  likely tagging slips
- Tag matching is case-insensitive
- API: new firefly.taggedTransactions() using Firefly's tag endpoint, with a fallback
  to a full transaction scan if that endpoint is unavailable
- Fix: Firefly pagination is now followed to the last page instead of silently
  keeping only the first — long windows no longer understate totals
- Chore: split-flattening extracted to one helper; formatters moved to client/src/format.js

[0.9.1]
- Fix: include transfer in default filterTypes, fix URL sync accordingly

[0.9.0]
- Feature: filter state syncs bidirectionally with URL search params — dashboard
  views are now shareable and survive a reload

[0.8.7]
- update readme regarding token settings

[0.8.6]
- Revert: client-side error message formatting (caused raw JSON parse errors to surface)
- Note: if you see auth errors, recreate your Personal Access Token in Firefly-III
  (Profile → OAuth → Personal Access Tokens)

[0.8.5]
- Fix: proxy now detects when Firefly-III redirects to login (expired/invalid token)
  and returns a clear HTTP 401 instead of a confusing JSON parse error
- Fix: guard against non-JSON responses from misconfigured reverse proxies
- Fix: error messages now include the Node.js error code (e.g. ECONNREFUSED),
  the target URL, and the raw detail — making connection issues actionable
- Chore: remove unused SESSION_SECRET from .env.example
